    <h1>Kiavi DSCR Loans, Explained</h1>
    <p class="lede">Kiavi's 30-year rental loan qualifies on the property's rent, not your personal income. Here's how the DSCR math works, what it costs, and when it beats a conventional investor mortgage.</p>

    <h2>What a DSCR loan is</h2>
    <p>DSCR stands for <strong>debt-service-coverage ratio</strong>: monthly rent divided by the full monthly payment (principal, interest, taxes, insurance, and HOA dues). A DSCR of 1.25 means the rent covers the payment with 25% to spare. Kiavi underwrites the property on that ratio — <strong>no W-2s, no tax returns, no DTI</strong> — which is why DSCR loans are the standard takeout for BRRRR investors and self-employed landlords.</p>

