    <h2>The flip-to-rental pipeline</h2>
    <p>The strongest reason to run a BRRRR through Kiavi is continuity: buy and rehab on a <a href="/kiavi-fix-and-flip/">Kiavi bridge loan</a>, then refinance into the DSCR loan with a lender that already has your file, your entity docs, and your draw history. One underwriting relationship, no re-explaining the deal, and the payoff timing is coordinated internally — see <a href="/faqs/kiavi-payoff-request/">how payoffs work</a>.</p>

    <h2>DSCR vs. conventional investor mortgage</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>DSCR wins</strong> when you're self-employed, already have 10 financed properties (Fannie's limit), close in an LLC, or can't document income cleanly.</li>
      <li><strong>Conventional wins</strong> on pure rate if you W-2 qualify easily and are under the property limit — typically 0.5–1.5 points cheaper.</li>
      <li><strong>Check the DSCR before you apply:</strong> our <a href="/kiavi-deal-calculator/">deal calculator</a> includes the rent-coverage math.</li>
    </ul>

